## Knowledge

@knowledge
Topic: Recursive descent vs line-based parsing
Difficulty: Intermediate
Prerequisites: Basic parsing theory
Summary:
XTXT does not nest, so a single line-based pass is enough. That is a
constraint on the format, not a limitation of the parser — and it is what
keeps a from-scratch implementation an afternoon's work.
@endknowledge

## An exchange worth keeping

@chat
Model: claude-opus-5
User: Why not just use Markdown with front matter?
Assistant:
Front matter is one record at the top of the file. XTXT lets a record sit
anywhere, next to the thing it describes, and names it. That is the whole
difference.
@endchat

